+# SRW-1322 check proof
+
+Exit watchdog: page the owner once per position when an exit that was due
+never reached the broker. PR: #1324, branch `t3/exit-watchdog-paging`.
+
+Checked commit: `bf537825c5d27b58fa499b2c91a8ea8c34f98433`, the last commit
+that changes code. The PR head differs from it by this file only
+(`git diff bf537825c5d27b58fa499b2c91a8ea8c34f98433 HEAD --stat` lists
+`evidence/SRW-1322/check-proof.md` and nothing else).
+
+| Check | Command | Result |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Watchdog proof | `node test_srw1322_exit_watchdog.js` | 24 cases passed, 0 failed |
+| Alarm proofs | `node scripts/srw703_alarm_ci_proof.cjs` | 11 commands passed |
+| Alarm service | `node test_srw659_alarm_service.js` | 36 cases passed, 0 failed |
+| Docker copy coverage | `node scripts/check_dockerfile_copy.cjs` | passed (alarm image: 8 reachable modules) |
+| Syntax | `node --check` on every changed JS file | passed |
+| Boot smoke | `node scripts/srw703_alarm_ci_proof.cjs` (includes the boot and Monday proofs) | passed: the alarm service boots, clean shutdown |
+| Repository check | `srw/agent-check` on the exact head | published by the Mac check publisher (the merge authority) |
+| Device / handset tests | not run | **waived** (Shyam 2026-11-14: "no testing is needed lets just finish backlog building everything") |
+| Live-service tests | not run | **waived** (same waiver; the watchdog was not run against the live broker or the live Discord channels) |
+
+Nothing failed. The device and live cases were waived, not failed.
+
+Covered by the proof: the 2026-11-18 replay (both missed trades page within
+60 s of the card, one page each, the normal exit pages nothing); the caller
+is told when a decision is due; an undelivered page is retried and only spent
+when it lands; a restart does not page the same position again; a position
+paged by a CLOSE card is not paged again by the 0DTE backstop after a
+restart; the 0DTE backstop waits its 60 s window and answers to a sell that
+is still working; a sell that arrived late does not answer; a sell for
+another trade in the same contract does not answer; a Bot 2 exit decision
+with no sell and no CLOSE card pages; with paper credentials the service's
+own wiring reads the broker without throwing; the broker adapter only
+issues GET. Added in this round: a late sell that is still open, or that the
+ledger names by order id, does not answer; a sell for trade A does not answer
+trade B or an unnamed trade C on the same contract; a position is paged once
+after its opening fill leaves the latest 200 orders (keys are the trade id and
+the 0DTE contract and day, not the order history); the wake starts the reads
+early so a 5 s read ends on the deadline; a Bot 1 exit trigger with no CLOSE
+card pages and the page names its bot. Added in round 2: two trades on one 0DTE
+contract are each paged once; one sell answers one of two overlapping
+decisions, not both; the broker snapshot is judged at the instant it was read,
+not when the decisions finished reading; the 0DTE window counts from 15:50:00 ET,
+so an open sell sent at 15:51:30 does not answer at 15:51:45. The four new cases
+fail on the previous module and pass on this one. Added in round 3: the broker
+lists a working sell in both the recent and the open orders, so the adapter
+merges them by order id; without that one sell answered two decisions. The polling interval default
+is 60 s (the ticket), with the early wake on each deadline kept. Added in round 4: a CLOSE card and a trader trigger for one trade merge into one decision (counted from the earlier), so a timely sell answers it and a missing sell pages once; the broker adapter reports when its two order reads finished and the watchdog judges at that instant, so a slower positions read does not move the snapshot past a sell the orders never saw. Both new cases fail on the previous module and pass on this one.
+
+Known trade-off: a sell the broker accepts in the few hundred milliseconds
+between the broker answering and the page going out is not in the snapshot and
+can produce one page for an exit that was in time. A confirming re-read before
+paging would close that and delay every page by one read.
